{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984813-indian-mtaw-darshanas-and-varna","id":984813,"title":"[Indian MtAw] Darshanas and Varna","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-10T04:30:07-07:00","id":984813,"title":"[Indian MtAw] Darshanas and Varna","content":"In <b>Dark Eras</b> <i>To the Strongest </i>chapter we have introduction of those era Indian Awakened - Great Cult of <i>Mantra Sadhaki</i>, Exiles from the Kingdom of Dragons - that base their myths on Naga Kingdom, popular in Indian Peninsula. Thing is that in that era concept of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Varna_(Hinduism)\" target=\"_blank\">Varna</a> - casts of Hindu society - is strongly present. Small sum up of those:<ul><li>the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brahmin\" target=\"_blank\">Brahmins</a>: priests, scholars and teachers.</li> <li>the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kshatriya\" target=\"_blank\">Kshatriyas</a>: rulers, warriors and administrators.</li> <li>the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaishya\" target=\"_blank\">Vaishyas</a>: cattle herders, agriculturists, artisans and merchants.</li> <li>the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shudra\" target=\"_blank\">Shudras</a>: laborers and service providers.</li> </ul>As easily seen, most Indian mages from this and all next eras would be from Brahmins cast, with few from Adamantine Arrow / Vajrastra Darshana. What about cults in other casts? How they relate from ancient to modern times to Diamond Orders and Seers of Throne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-10-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T04:40:24-07:00","id":984818,"title":"","content":"It says explicitly that they reject caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T04:53:14-07:00","id":984822,"title":"","content":"<i>Mantra Sadhaki </i>reject castes - but Awakened after creating Orders changed this Great Cult to be not totally relevant ( by unifying them with 'Atlantean' Westerners ). Creation of Mysterium should also change things in India. And finally of Free Council - but those events come after British colonization, so 'Western' Orders spread should work just fine then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-10-2016, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T05:08:31-07:00","id":984826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984813-indian-mtaw-darshanas-and-varna?p=984822#post984822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Mantra Sadhaki </i>reject castes - but Awakened after creating Orders changed this Great Cult to be not totally relevant ( by unifying them with 'Atlantean' Westerners ).</div> </div> </div> </div>The major problem is the Awakening doesn't respect caste. The personal rejection of caste is a practical measure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:44:48-07:00","id":984872,"title":"","content":"Without getting into a whole real-world debate about this: many academics argue that the varnas were significantly more fluid at different points in Indian history, particularly pre-colonization. If I were running a Mage game in an Indian setting, I would definitely not map the Paths/Orders to caste. It's a pretty huge part of the setting for me in any era that Awakening reveals the emptiness of Fallen power structures by being open to anyone. A person outside/below the caste system is equally if not more likely to Awaken than someone inhabiting the high castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:49:15-07:00","id":984873,"title":"","content":"What Michael said; Awakening arrives like a bolt from the blue and can strike anyone, regardless of caste. If the Awakened tried to maintain old prejudices after Awakening, they'd struggle to maintain converts. The Silver Ladder certainly has a caste system of sorts, but it is adamantly not your birth that determines it.<br /> <br /> Seers might hold onto the caste system, adding that they are the highest, most secret caste or some such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:52:00-07:00","id":984876,"title":"","content":"Yeah - we very deliberately didn't map Awakened groups to varnas because to do so would be to open the racist door. It's both lazy and a minefield, and in-world Awakening definitely doesn't respect position in Sleeper society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:49:44-07:00","id":984901,"title":"","content":"My take is, I could easily see is Indian Diamond/Seer mages - inspired by Hindu or Buddhist traditions - seeing awakening as a type of reincarnation that erases your past caste. Only your new &quot;caste&quot; within the Atlantean Orders matters, but none of the Orders neatly map to Hindu Varna, and your Sleeper Varna does not in any way predestine you for a particular Awakened Order. They'd perhaps look down on the nameless but only consider apostates, the mad, banishers, and scelesti as truly &quot;untouchable&quot;. The Shudra &quot;equivalent&quot; would likely be Sleepers, not any type of mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:02:49-07:00","id":986019,"title":"","content":"I invented these. While I would hardly call them representative of anything historical -- they are as fictional as the future Diamond -- it isn't really true to the source to map abilities to jati or varna. Drona is a priest, but he kicks ass, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:06:03-07:00","id":986020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984813-indian-mtaw-darshanas-and-varna?p=986019#post986019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drona is a priest, but he kicks ass, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not recall this term - where is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:30:01-07:00","id":986025,"title":"","content":"Drona is a name, not a term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}